# One maintainer, so this is not about routing. It is about the review never
# being skipped by accident on the parts where a mistake is expensive and
# invisible.
*                           @impressiver

# Consent and capture. Section 5 of the spec is the promise the app makes about
# what is recorded and when; a change here can weaken it without any test
# noticing, because the tests assert the rules as written.
/Sources/SnittCapture/      @impressiver
/Sources/SnittAutomation/   @impressiver

# Signing, notarization and the update channel. These install code on other
# people's machines.
/Scripts/release.sh         @impressiver
/Scripts/notarize.sh        @impressiver
/Scripts/make-app.sh        @impressiver
/Scripts/make-appcast.sh    @impressiver

# The decision log. Reversing a decision is allowed; doing it silently leaves
# every later reader working from a premise that is no longer true.
/docs/superpowers/specs/    @impressiver

# CI runs on pull requests from forks. A workflow change is a change to what
# runs against untrusted code.
/.github/                   @impressiver
